{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794238078,"nonce":"NClSYBQCpZKsaAyzHensqbEvs2Y=","title":"The N1E surface-load pattern ignores the operands of the cross product","message":"_n1e_surface_load_spec accepts inner(g, cross(...)) whenever the cross contains the test function, and the assembler then always uses phi x n with the mesh normal. cross(n, v) (= -v x n), cross(n, cross(v, n)) (the tangential trace) or a cross with any other vector are silently assembled as v x n. _n1e_surface_mass_spec has the same shape: inner(cross(u, n), cross(n, v)) is assembled as +(n x u).(n x v), with the wrong sign.\n\nFix direction: check that the cross is (test, region normal) in that order, and route anything else to the general boundary path or raise.","files":null}]}